<title>DENMARK: Danish April current account surplus 0.1 bln DKK.</title>
<headline>Danish April current account surplus 0.1 bln DKK.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's current account edged into a 0.1 billion crown surplus in April 1997 the national statistics office said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>The April surplus compared with a revised 1.5 billion crown deficit for March.</p>
<p>DANISH CURRENT ACCOUNT (billions of crowns)</p>
<p>	    April 1997	  March 1997	April 1996</p>
<p>		+0.1		-1.5 (-1.3)*    +1.795 (+1.0)*</p>
<p>*Revised (original figures in brackets)</p>
<p>Cumulative figures for the past three, six and 12 month periods as per end-March:</p>
<p>(Billions of crowns)  Three-month Six-month Twelve-month</p>
<p>Current account		   +0.7     -3.4	 +7.9</p>
<p>Goods				 +9.2    +18.6	+41.1</p>
<p>Services			    -0.2     -0.4	 +5.3</p>
<p>Interest, other		   -8.3    -21.6	-38.5</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are subject to rounding. Nine market analysts polled by Reuters had predicted an average April current account surplus of 1.0 billion crowns.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33-969652</p>
</text>
